@LBA2_PRODUCT_NAME@ - PlayStation Vita homebrew

Install lba2cc-vita.vpk with VitaShell. Title ID: @LBA2_VITA_TITLE_ID@.
This package contains no retail game assets.

Copy files from your legally owned LBA2 installation to ux0:/data/lba2/.
Put LBA2.HQR and the other retail HQR files directly in that directory.
Keep the installation's Music/, VIDEO/ and VOX/ folders and their contents.

Settings, saves and logs: ux0:/data/lba2cc/user/
Back up this directory before upgrading. Reinstalling the VPK does not
replace it or the retail data. Use the game's Quit option to exit cleanly.

The SDL2 GXM renderer scales the software framebuffer to 960x544 with
letterboxing. No shader compiler plugin is needed for this renderer.
Left stick: move forward/backward and turn. L: behaviour. R: throw.
Triangle: inventory. Square: action. Cross: always-action. Circle: return.
Start: menu. Select: holomap. Right stick: camera. D-pad: spells.
Dodge is unbound because the handheld has no stick-click buttons.
Existing explicit gamepad bindings in lba2.cfg take precedence.
Custom save-name keyboard entry and touch controls are not added.
Further hardware validation remains required.

Diagnostic builds (--diagnostics when building)
----------------------------------------------
The game creates its user directory automatically.
Diagnostic builds also write ux0:/data/lba2cc-boot.log before SDL starts.
This file is replaced each launch; preserve it after a failed boot.
For optional DEBUGNET streaming, put the receiver computer's LAN IPv4 address
in ux0:/data/lba2cc-debugnet.txt. Receive on that computer's UDP port 18194.
No console plugin is required. Use only a trusted LAN; logs are unencrypted.
Missing receiver configuration disables network output, not local capture.
